1-08","stage19_causal_queue":"1968-11-08"},"source_ladder_exhausted_proposed":[],"status":"MACHINE DRAFT - UNVERIFIED; not a claim; see jobs/claim-drafts/AGENT_GUIDE.md"},"claim":{"instrument_id":"EO:11434","later_source_search":[],"operative_clauses":[{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"it is ordered as follows :\nS ection  .1. Policies and Regulations.  The Secretary of State with \nrespect to the Foreign Service personnel and retirement systems and \nthe Director of the United States Information Agency with respect \nto the Foreign Service personnel system of the United States Informa­\ntion Agency shall promulgate policies and related regulations govern­\ning such systems after consultation with the Director of the Bureau \nof the Budget and the Chairman of the Civil Service Commission.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"33 FR 16485, PDF pages 5-6; operative words before the numbered sections","sha256":"5e7daa00b7de02255c7a84165a24dde0a24006b011f4824ef936299ccfb2a8e6","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1968-11-13/pdf/FR-1968-11-13.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11434#preamble-op","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 2. B oard  o f the Foreign Service and B oard  o f Exam iners fo r  \nthe Foreign Service.  The Board of the Foreign Service and the Board \nof Examiners for the Foreign Service established by Executive Order \nNo. 11264 of December 31,1965, as hereinafter amended, shall exercise \nwith respect to Foreign Service information officers the functions \ndelegated to them by that order with respect to Foreign Service officers. \nThe Boards Shall perform such additional functions with respect to \nForeign Service personnel of the United States Information Agency \nas the Director may from time to time delegate or otherwise assign.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"33 FR 16485, PDF pages 5-6; Sec. 2","sha256":"5e7daa00b7de02255c7a84165a24dde0a24006b011f4824ef936299ccfb2a8e6","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1968-11-13/pdf/FR-1968-11-13.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11434#sec2","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 3. Foreign Service Retirem ent and D isability System.  The \nauthority vested in the President by Sections 9 (b) and 16(a) of Public \nLaw 90-494 to prescribe regulations relating to participation of For­\neign Service staff officers and employees of the United States Informa­\ntion Agency and Foreign Service Reserve officers with unlimited \ntenure, respectively, in the Foreign Service Retirement and Disability \nSystem is hereby delegated to the Secretary of State.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"33 FR 16485, PDF pages 5-6; Sec. 3","sha256":"5e7daa00b7de02255c7a84165a24dde0a24006b011f4824ef936299ccfb2a8e6","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1968-11-13/pdf/FR-1968-11-13.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11434#sec3","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 4. Amendment o f Executive Order No. 1126If..  Section 21 of \nExecutive Order No. 11264 of December 31, 1965, is amended as \nfollows :","original_source":{"page_or_item":"33 FR 16485, PDF pages 5-6; Sec. 4 (lead-in)","sha256":"5e7daa00b7de02255c7a84165a24dde0a24006b011f4824ef936299ccfb2a8e6","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1968-11-13/pdf/FR-1968-11-13.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11434#sec4","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) Paragraph (2) of subsection (b) is amended by deleting < c (iii) \nThe United States Information Agency” and redesignating subdivi­\nsion (iv) as subdivision (iii).","original_source":{"page_or_item":"33 FR 16485, PDF pages 5-6; Sec. 4(a)","sha256":"5e7daa00b7de02255c7a84165a24dde0a24006b011f4824ef936299ccfb2a8e6","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1968-11-13/pdf/FR-1968-11-13.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11434#sec4(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) Paragraph (3) of subsection (b) is redesignated as paragraph\n(4) and the following new paragraph (3) is added:\n“ (3) Two officials of the United States Information Agency who \nshall be designated as members of the Board by the Director of the \nUnited States Information Agency.”\nFEDERAL REQISTER, VOL. 33, NO. 221— WEDNESDAY, NOVEMBER 13, 1968\n\n=== PDF page 6 of 72 ===\n16486 THE PRESIDENT\n(c) Subsection (d) is amended by substituting “subsection (b) (1),\n(b )(2 ) or ( b ) (3 )” for “subsection (b )(1 ) or (b )(2 ).”","original_source":{"page_or_item":"33 FR 16485, PDF pages 5-6; Sec. 4(b)","sha256":"5e7daa00b7de02255c7a84165a24dde0a24006b011f4824ef936299ccfb2a8e6","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1968-11-13/pdf/FR-1968-11-13.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11434#sec4(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 5. E ffective Date.  This order shall be effective as of August 20, \n1968, and the Secretary of State and the Director of the United States \nInformation Agency, m their discretion and consistent with law, may \nmake rules and regulations pursuant to this order effective on or \nafter that date.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"33 FR 16485, PDF pages 5-6; Sec. 5","sha256":"5e7daa00b7de02255c7a84165a24dde0a24006b011f4824ef936299ccfb2a8e6","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1968-11-13/pdf/FR-1968-11-13.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11434#sec5","state_at_cutoff":null}],"original_representation":{"page_or_item":"33 FR 16485, PDF pages 5-6","sha256":"5e7daa00b7de02255c7a84165a24dde0a24006b011f4824ef936299ccfb2a8e6","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1968-11-13/pdf/FR-1968-11-13.pdf"},"research_rationale":"","savings_residuals":null,"schema":"eo-lifecycle-claim/v1","unresolved_material_gaps":["DRAFT: state_at_cutoff not decided for 7 clause(s); clause inventory completeness not confirmed","DRAFT: whole-order ending not established","DRAFT: savings and residual effects not closed","DRAFT: later_source_search not recorded (machine searches are proposals only; paste them after judging them adequate and resolving every CONFLICT line)","CONFLICT FULL_AND_PARTIAL_EVIDENCE_CONFLICT: EO:12363: the sources read as both a whole and a partial ending"],"whole_order_end":null,"whole_order_status":"no"},"draft_schema":"eo-claim-draft/v1","instrument_id":"EO:11434"}
